{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788216824,"nonce":"XokQ3UdNrl3PqQUUWA1hyPiOIck=","message":"WORKER — 4.2 authored on branch spec/4.2-play-loop (commit 2bbcd7c, BORGES,\nsession 9). Deliverables: playbook/PLAY-LOOP.md (the skill), SESSION-START.md\nposition 10 (colony notes), accept/4.2-play-loop.{md,py} (mechanical audit of\na finished run dir + selftest). Not merged; audit requested before continuing.\n\nOPEN QUESTIONS, RESOLVED WITH RATIONALE\n\n1. Skill vs prompt-doc packaging: PROMPT DOC, playbook/PLAY-LOOP.md.\nInvestigated rather than preferred: .gitignore ignores `.claude/` in this\nrepo, and DESIGN §Learning stakes the playbook on git inheritance — \"every\nagent instance starts with everything ever learned\". A .claude skill file\nhere would be invisible to a fresh clone and to Dorian's diffs, failing the\none property that matters; the workspace's /triage-errors conventions live on\nthe other box and were not verifiable from BORGES, so I did not imitate them\nblind. The body is runner-agnostic markdown; any box wanting /play-colony\npoints a one-line local skill at the file. The spec pre-authorized this fork\n(\"or prompt doc if skills don't fit the runner\") — the runner it doesn't fit\nis git, which is the runner that counts.\n\n2. Cadence tuning: default `advance --until.letter --timeout_ticks 60000`\n(any-letter, one-day cap); 2500-tick advances (proposed) or until.event\ninside emergencies; no minimum. All guards written against the shipped\nmatcher set {ticks|letter|threat|alert|event} — no condition matcher until\n1.6, per the verification. max_tps left to the mod's thermal cap. The cap\ndecision is below under THE DAILY.MD ASSUMPTION.\n\n3. State between sessions: YES, one file per colony —\nRUNS/\u003ccolony\u003e.colony.md, loaded at new SESSION-START position 10, updated as\nthe session's last act. Holds only what nothing else records: intents,\nhalf-done projects, landmark rationale, deferred decisions. Hard boundary:\nnever lessons — learning goes through postmortem.md into the playbook, or the\nnotes become a shadow playbook nobody audits. The last-seq handoff lives in\nthe run summary (a per-run fact), not the notes, so position 9 reads it from\nthe newest summary and position 10 stays pure intent.\n\nTHE DAILY.MD ASSUMPTION — HONOURED, AND NAMED AS LOAD-BEARING\n\nchecklists/README.md justifies the daily rung on \"the 4.2 loop already caps\nearly advances at about one in-game day\". PLAY-LOOP.md §Cadence honours it\nand strengthens it from \"early on\" to standing policy (proposed): the advance\ncap doubles as the daily sweep's sampling interval, since daily items run at\nthe first read after a boundary and their staleness is bounded by the longest\nadvance. Raising the cap is therefore a recorded policy change whose commit\nmust either re-justify daily.md's items at the new latency or move the\nintolerant ones onto 1.6 conditions. The assumption is not silently unmet; it\nis printed on the knob.\n\nAMENDMENTS AND VERIFICATION, EACH CLOSED IN THE TEXT\n\n- Undraft hole (comment 1): closed twice — raid-end's step 3 stays, and the\n  loop adds a pre-advance gate (no advance while any colonist is drafted\n  absent live hostiles; digest flags, pawns {cap:200} confirm when\n  colonists.more \u003e 0) so the discipline survives raid-end's retirement into\n  cc8988c. Invariant 4, auditable.\n- Dialog halts (comments 2/3): first-class turn input. With 3.5 verbs: read\n  halted_on, decide, act, log. Without: never retry — summary, then escalate\n  with the halted_on payload verbatim (1.7's visible-and-stuck is stated as\n  designed, not corruption). Wedge rule pinned at N=2 consecutive 0-tick\n  advances, whatever the reasons: the first 0-tick return demands a state\n  change, the second proves there wasn't one. Checked mechanically by the\n  auditor from the transcript's advance envelopes.\n- Addition 2 (uncheckable invariant): adopted 4.1's ledger as the fix;\n  colony-start steps get ids colony-start-\u003cn\u003e so the numbered list is\n  diffable too. The auditor diffs daily coverage per day snapshot.\n- Addition 3 (digest not uniformly cheap): §read — one digest per return,\n  not per thought, with the room-Role recompute named.\n- Sections-not-firehose (comment 2): §think — pawns is the staple, pawn\n  drill-down names its sections, opinions stays off in routine turns.\n- Acceptance made mechanical per the verification: transcript completeness =\n  per-op counts vs the journal's own action/dev record; the threat day must\n  end at zero drafted; \"reviewed for compliance\" labelled a human gate.\n\nTWO RESOLUTIONS MADE IN PASSING, FLAGGED FOR THE AUDIT\n\n- No load/newgame verb exists (checked the registry), so \"resume or newgame\n  per args\" is launcher-owned in the skill (run-agent.sh / autostart), with\n  menu/down verdicts mapping to relaunch-or-escalate per machine rules. Not\n  filed as a verb gap: a supported path exists and loading mid-protocol was\n  deliberately left outside it.\n- accept/4.2-play-loop.py's selftest has NOT been run — BORGES has no\n  python, the same constraint that produced this directory's .ps1 drivers.\n  First command on the bench box: python accept/4.2-play-loop.py --selftest.\n  Desk-checked only; the acceptance note says so in those words.\n\nNOT DEMONSTRATED, in those words: no session was run against a live bench —\nno checklist ledger, transcript, summary or post-mortem exists from this\nskill yet; the emergency posture, the dialog rule and the undraft gate are\nspecified and audited-for, not exercised. RimWorld was never launched. That\ndemonstration is 4.3's, by design.","files":null}]}